    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [x] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [x] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n- [x] I have updated 'mini.nvim' to latest version of the `main` branch\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.pairs\n\n### Neovim version\n\n0.11 (!at least latest Nightly build!)\n\n### Description\n\nWhen writing the closing character for my custom pairs (`¿?` and `¡!`), neovim writes the opening symbol (`¿` and `¡` respectively). I would expect to get `?` when typing it by itself, instead I get `¿`.\n\n\n\n### Reproduction\n\n1. Setup `mini.pairs` defining the two custom pairs I mentioned.\n\n```lua\n  require('mini.pairs').setup({\n    mappings = {\n      ['¿'] = { action = 'open', pair = '¿?', neigh_pattern = '[^\\\\].' },\n      ['¡'] = { action = 'open', pair = '¡!', neigh_pattern = '[^\\\\].' },\n      ['?'] = { action = 'close', pair = '¿?', neigh_pattern = '[^\\\\].' },\n      ['!'] = { action = 'close', pair = '¡!', neigh_pattern = '[^\\\\].' },\n    }\n  })\n```\n\n2. In a new session, try and write `?`. The result is that `¿` gets type instead. Forcing the literal input with `<C-v>` does yield the expected `?` so it is not an issue with my keyboard layout. \n\nIs there something wrong with my usage of the module?",
