        {
            "author_association": "NONE",
            "body": "Ohh, got it! A workaround I found for now is to set it up as:\n\n```lua\n  require('mini.pairs').setup({\n    mappings = {\n      ['¿'] = { action = 'open', pair = '¿?', neigh_pattern = '[^\\\\].' },\n      ['¡'] = { action = 'open', pair = '¡!', neigh_pattern = '[^\\\\].' },\n    }\n  })\n```\n\nIt auto-closes correctly with `¿` but does not ignore typing the closing `?` if auto-closed, in that case I just go to normal mode and move around.\n\nI understand your concerns with performance, no worries. Btw just wishing you all the best in your endeavors, `mini.nvim`  has replaced basically every other plugin in my setup.",
